# opencode-acp-adapter: `--server` value is never validated — a trailing `--server` silently talks to the default serve, `--server=` / a flag-like value loop forever on "Failed to parse URL", and a typo'd flag is silently ignored

## Summary

`bin/opencode-acp-adapter.mjs` takes its one operator flag, `--server`, with no validation at all. In `parseServerUrl` (lines 64–76 at `def55caf48`):

```js
function parseServerUrl(argv) {
  let server = process.env.OPENCODE_ACP_SERVER || 'http://127.0.0.1:13420';
  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {
    if (argv[i] === '--server' && argv[i + 1]) {
      server = argv[i + 1];
      i += 1;
    } else if (argv[i].startsWith('--server=')) {
      server = argv[i].slice('--server='.length);
    }
  }
  return server.replace(/\/+$/, '');
}
```

- A **trailing** `--server` fails the `argv[i + 1]` truthiness check and is silently dropped — the adapter talks to the default `http://127.0.0.1:13420` serve (or the env var) instead of the server the operator meant to name, with no warning anywhere.
- **`--server=`** sets `server` to the empty string. Every request becomes a relative URL: the event stream (`runEventStream`, lines 226–257) logs `Failed to parse URL from /api/event; reconnecting` and retries every 1s forever, and session calls fail the same way — yet ACP `initialize` still succeeds, so the gateway sees a healthy agent whose every session is broken.
- A **flag-like value** (`--server --bogus-flag`) is consumed verbatim as the URL: `Failed to parse URL from --bogus-flag/api/event; reconnecting`, same infinite loop.
- A **typo'd flag** (`--sever http://127.0.0.1:9`) matches nothing in the loop and is silently ignored — again the default serve, no signal.

`parseServerUrl` is not exported and has no unit coverage: `bin/opencode-acp-adapter.test.mjs` only ever passes a well-formed `--server http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (line 105).

## Evidence (verified this run, laptop, origin/main `def55caf484833e062247c46e5b0c4bb719accd3`)

Probe `~/git/fleet/probe-acp-server-arg/` — the real module on the laptop primary (md5 `bd0bdaccb8c47bd031bb82a6b8149d08`), driven over stdio JSON-RPC (`initialize` + `session/new`) with `OPENCODE_ACP_ADAPTER_DEBUG=1`; the startup debug line prints the resolved `serverBase`:

| Invocation | Observed |
|---|---|
| control: `--server http://127.0.0.1:9` | `started; server=http://127.0.0.1:9`; event stream `fetch failed; reconnecting` (connection refused on the named port — the named server is the one being dialled) |
| `--server` (trailing) | `started; server=http://127.0.0.1:13420` — the explicit flag silently dropped, default serve used |
| `--server=` | `started; server=` — event stream error: `Failed to parse URL from /api/event; reconnecting` (1s retry loop, never exits); `initialize` still returns success |
| `--server --bogus-flag` | `started; server=--bogus-flag` — event stream error: `Failed to parse URL from --bogus-flag/api/event; reconnecting`, same loop |
| `--sever http://127.0.0.1:9` (typo) | `started; server=http://127.0.0.1:13420` — unknown flag silently ignored, default serve used |

## Why it matters

This adapter is the bridge between the ACP gateway (acpx/OpenClaw) and the standing OpenCode serve: prompts, sessions, and the server password resolved in `serverPassword()` all go to whatever `serverBase` resolves to. Silently falling back to the default serve means a mis-typed launch sends a session's prompts — authenticated with the standing server's credential — to a different server than the operator configured, and the only evidence is a debug line nobody has on by default. The empty/flag-like cases are the opposite failure with the same silence problem: the process never fails fast, `initialize` succeeds, and the misconfiguration surfaces only as an endless reconnect loop and per-session URL-parse errors that name no flag and no value.

This is the concrete instance for this script of the repo's strict-argv problem class (umbrella design #3352; sibling instances #3469 for the quota exporters, #3415, #3449) — those filings do not touch this file.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `--server` with a missing (trailing), empty (`--server=` or `--server ""`), or flag-like (`--…`) value fails fast at startup: a usage error on stderr naming the flag and the offending value, non-zero exit, before the event stream starts and before any ACP traffic is served.
- [ ] A `--server` value that is not a parseable `http:`/`https:` URL fails the same way at startup — never as a per-request `Failed to parse URL` reconnect loop.
- [ ] The valid forms keep working unchanged: `--server <url>`, `--server=<url>`, trailing slashes stripped, `OPENCODE_ACP_SERVER` env fallback, and the built-in default when neither is given.
- [ ] Regression tests in `bin/opencode-acp-adapter.test.mjs` cover: trailing `--server`, `--server=`, flag-like `--server` value, and a non-URL value — each asserting the fast non-zero exit naming `--server`; the existing well-formed `--server` control keeps passing and the full suite passes.
- [ ] Unknown-argument handling (e.g. the `--sever` typo) follows the contract chosen under #3352 — at minimum it must not silently change which server is dialled without a stderr signal.

Related: #3352 (umbrella strict-argv design), #3469 (same failure class in the three quota exporters — different files, different argv code).
